menu "GALPANEL features"

config GALPANEL_ENDPOINT_LED
    bool "Use AUX LED to show the active output endpoint"
    depends on SHIELD_GALPANEL
    default y
    help
      Turn the AUX LED on while the currently selected HID endpoint is USB.
      Turn it off while the selected endpoint is BLE or no endpoint is ready.

config GALPANEL_STATUS_INDICATORS
    bool "Enable GALPANEL status indicators"
    depends on SHIELD_GALPANEL || SHIELD_GALPANEL_STATUS_TEST || SHIELD_GALPANEL_SAFETY_TEST
    default y
    select GPIO
    help
      Drive LINK, INFO, FN and AUX from ZMK state and provide the optional
      WARN long-press safety test.

config GALPANEL_LINK_ON_MS
    int "BLE LINK LED on time after connection (milliseconds)"
    depends on GALPANEL_STATUS_INDICATORS
    range 0 600000
    default 0
    help
      A value of zero keeps LINK on while connected. A positive value turns
      LINK off after that many milliseconds while preserving the connected
      state in firmware. The final GALPANEL firmware uses 30000.

config GALPANEL_PROFILE_NAMES
    bool "Use GALPANEL N names for BLE profiles"
    depends on SHIELD_GALPANEL || SHIELD_GALPANEL_STATUS_TEST || SHIELD_GALPANEL_SAFETY_TEST
    default y
    help
      Rename the active BLE advertising name to GALPANEL 1 through GALPANEL 5
      when the active profile changes.

config GALPANEL_SAFETY_TEST
    bool "Enable guarded GALPANEL SYS controls"
    depends on SHIELD_GALPANEL || SHIELD_GALPANEL_SAFETY_TEST
    default n
    help
      Own the SYS key so a tap selects the next BLE profile, a double tap
      toggles USB/BLE output, and a guarded six-second hold clears the current
      BLE profile bond with LED feedback.

config GALPANEL_NAME_RESET
    bool "Enable one-shot historical GALPANEL name reset"
    depends on SHIELD_GALPANEL_NAME_RESET
    default y
    help
      Write the historical static BLE name GALPANEL to the persistent
      settings area. This is a diagnostic/recovery image only.

endmenu
